WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.650
<v Narrator>Field reps live between meetings, and the CRM lives on a laptop.

2
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.353
<v Narrator>So the briefing gets skipped, and the notes wait until tonight.

3
00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:13.310
<v Narrator>Alex just calls the record desk.

4
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.514
<v Narrator>Reps call the record desk straight from Teams,

5
00:00:22.594 --> 00:00:26.710
<v Narrator>or dial its Teams number from their mobile, through Teams Phone extensibility.

6
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.947
<v Narrator>Azure Communication Services Call Automation bridges the audio to Voice Live,

7
00:00:32.027 --> 00:00:34.890
<v Narrator>where GPT Realtime holds the conversation.

8
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.520
<v Narrator>Your server verifies the rep, reads and writes the CRM,

9
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.170
<v Narrator>and passes what it can't change to Sales Operations in Teams.

10
00:00:44.592 --> 00:00:49.012
<v Narrator>Alex is on his way to see Fabrikam, and calls the record desk from his mobile.

11
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.525
<v Agent>This is the Contoso sales assistant, an automated agent.

12
00:00:53.605 --> 00:00:56.680
<v Agent>Please enter your six-digit Contoso sales PIN.

13
00:00:58.021 --> 00:01:01.705
<v Narrator>Caller ID matches his registered mobile, but that's only a hint.

14
00:01:01.785 --> 00:01:05.811
<v Narrator>Nothing opens until your server checks his PIN against a stored hash.

15
00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.940
<v Agent>Thanks, Alex, you're verified. Which account?

16
00:01:11.247 --> 00:01:12.717
<v Alex>Brief me on Fabrikam

17
00:01:13.047 --> 00:01:16.096
<v Agent>Fabrikam, Strategic tier, your account.

18
00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:20.023
<v Agent>Last touch was a call on May 2 about pilot rollout.

19
00:01:20.103 --> 00:01:25.282
<v Agent>3 open deals: enterprise renewal at about 250 thousand, in Negotiation,

20
00:01:25.362 --> 00:01:29.941
<v Agent>closing June 30, renewal services add-on at about 42 thousand,

21
00:01:30.021 --> 00:01:35.466
<v Agent>in Proposal, closing July 10, and analytics expansion at about 80 thousand,

22
00:01:35.546 --> 00:01:38.062
<v Agent>in Proposal, closing August 18.

23
00:01:38.142 --> 00:01:42.256
<v Agent>One task is due today: send the security questionnaire.

24
00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:45.797
<v Agent>Your contact is Dana Ruiz, VP of Operations.

25
00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:51.115
<v Narrator>Your server wrote that briefing, from accounts Alex owns or works on.

26
00:01:51.195 --> 00:01:53.718
<v Narrator>Phone numbers stay off it until he asks.

27
00:01:54.523 --> 00:01:55.923
<v Alex>What's Dana's number?

28
00:01:56.238 --> 00:02:02.128
<v Agent>Dana Ruiz's number is 206 555 0120.

29
00:02:04.201 --> 00:02:07.391
<v Narrator>Straight after the meeting, Alex calls back from Teams.

30
00:02:07.471 --> 00:02:10.481
<v Narrator>His Teams sign-in verifies him, so there's no PIN.

31
00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:16.587
<v Agent>Hi Alex, I'm the Contoso sales assistant, an automated agent. Which account?

32
00:02:17.931 --> 00:02:19.613
<v Alex>Log the Fabrikam meeting.

33
00:02:19.693 --> 00:02:21.910
<v Alex>Dana agreed to the renewal at 240k,

34
00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.594
<v Alex>moving to Closed Won pending signature, close date June 15th.

35
00:02:25.674 --> 00:02:28.131
<v Alex>Remind me to send the contract Friday.

36
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.618
<v Agent>Here's what I have for Fabrikam.

37
00:02:30.698 --> 00:02:33.348
<v Agent>A meeting activity with Dana Ruiz, today.

38
00:02:33.428 --> 00:02:36.968
<v Agent>Enterprise renewal: stage from Negotiation to Closed Won,

39
00:02:37.048 --> 00:02:39.698
<v Agent>amount from 250 thousand to 240 thousand,

40
00:02:39.778 --> 00:02:42.093
<v Agent>close date from June 30 to June 15,

41
00:02:42.173 --> 00:02:46.048
<v Agent>and next step from Security questionnaire to Pending signature.

42
00:02:46.128 --> 00:02:50.250
<v Agent>A task for you to send the contract, due Friday, June 12. Save it?

43
00:02:51.586 --> 00:02:53.754
<v Narrator>The model only passed Alex's words along.

44
00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.681
<v Narrator>Your server picked out each field,

45
00:02:55.761 --> 00:02:58.926
<v Narrator>checked it against your allow-list, and wrote that read-back.

46
00:02:59.686 --> 00:03:01.438
<v Narrator>A bare yes wouldn't count.

47
00:03:01.518 --> 00:03:05.694
<v Narrator>Even after “yes, save it”, your server holds the write for six seconds,

48
00:03:05.774 --> 00:03:07.606
<v Narrator>and “wait” still stops it.

49
00:03:08.394 --> 00:03:09.514
<v Alex>Yes, save it.

50
00:03:09.842 --> 00:03:13.382
<v Agent>Saving in six seconds. Say "wait" to stop it.

51
00:03:14.847 --> 00:03:16.897
<v Agent>Saved to Fabrikam's record.

52
00:03:18.253 --> 00:03:23.137
<v Narrator>Nobody objected, so your server wrote it all in one commit, an audit row per field.

53
00:03:23.217 --> 00:03:25.563
<v Narrator>“Undo that” would still reverse it.

54
00:03:27.632 --> 00:03:31.239
<v Narrator>Now Alex asks for changes only Sales Operations may make.

55
00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:35.232
<v Narrator>What a call can change is set by your server, not the prompt.

56
00:03:36.257 --> 00:03:41.027
<v Alex>Raise Fabrikam's credit limit to 500k and move them to net 60 payment terms.

57
00:03:41.324 --> 00:03:42.224
<v Agent>The credit limit

58
00:03:42.304 --> 00:03:45.531
<v Agent>and the payment terms aren't on the list of things I can change by phone,

59
00:03:45.611 --> 00:03:48.511
<v Agent>so nothing was written. Contoso Sales Operations can change them.

60
00:03:48.591 --> 00:03:50.714
<v Agent>Want me to put you through with the details?

61
00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:55.483
<v Narrator>Your server refused both fields, whatever the model made of them.

62
00:03:55.563 --> 00:03:58.104
<v Narrator>And your routing config decides who picks up.

63
00:03:58.998 --> 00:04:00.078
<v Alex>Yes, put me through.

64
00:04:00.417 --> 00:04:04.197
<v Agent>Putting you through to Contoso Sales Operations with the details.

65
00:04:05.568 --> 00:04:09.234
<v Narrator>Sales Operations' Teams queue rings, with the account,

66
00:04:09.314 --> 00:04:14.268
<v Narrator>the request and the refusal in the VoIP headers. No PIN, no phone numbers.

67
00:04:16.338 --> 00:04:20.228
<v Narrator>Last call: someone has Alex's phone, but not his PIN.

68
00:04:21.089 --> 00:04:24.654
<v Agent>This is the Contoso sales assistant, an automated agent.

69
00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.809
<v Agent>Please enter your six-digit Contoso sales PIN.

70
00:04:29.151 --> 00:04:32.169
<v Agent>I couldn't verify you, so I can't open any records.

71
00:04:32.249 --> 00:04:35.241
<v Agent>I'll put you through to Contoso Sales Operations.

72
00:04:36.574 --> 00:04:38.961
<v Narrator>No second try, and no record opened.

73
00:04:39.041 --> 00:04:43.864
<v Narrator>Sales Operations gets only the failed check and the number's last four digits.

74
00:04:46.281 --> 00:04:48.941
<v Narrator>These numbers come straight from the audit log.

75
00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:52.080
<v Narrator>The model talked; your server decided who was verified,

76
00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.501
<v Narrator>what was read out and what was written.

77
00:04:56.137 --> 00:05:00.792
<v Narrator>The model holds the conversation and passes the rep's words to server tools.

78
00:05:00.872 --> 00:05:04.817
<v Narrator>Fields, record IDs and transfer targets come from your server.

79
00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:08.284
<v Narrator>Your server verifies the caller, scopes every record,

80
00:05:08.364 --> 00:05:10.773
<v Narrator>checks each field against the allow-list,

81
00:05:10.853 --> 00:05:13.747
<v Narrator>holds the undo window, and writes the audit rows.

82
00:05:15.947 --> 00:05:20.140
<v Narrator>Making it yours is mostly configuration: the fields a call may change,

83
00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:23.287
<v Narrator>your reps, and who answers for Sales Operations.

84
00:05:23.737 --> 00:05:26.289
<v Narrator>Your CRM plugs in behind one adapter.

85
00:05:26.369 --> 00:05:31.107
<v Narrator>The spec, the tests and this demo script give your coding agent the rest.

86
00:05:33.707 --> 00:05:36.199
<v Narrator>Customer record lookup and update.

87
00:05:36.279 --> 00:05:41.667
<v Narrator>Run it in simulation in two minutes, then connect your own Teams number and CRM.
